  "query_preview": "../Saturday through Monday/... \nDrier weather is expected into the weekend as offshore flow will \nbecome predominate Saturday into Sunday with high pressure \nbeginning to build over the gulf. Late Friday into Saturday, a low\npressure system will quickly move south of the panhandle. This, \nalong with high pressure over the Yukon, will increase the \npressure gradient which in turn will increase wind speeds. \nStrongest wind speeds will most likely be across the northern \ninner channels, including Taku Inlet, with northerly winds around \n20 kts possible. The low pressure system to the south still looks \nto be on the weaker side which could prevent winds getting any \nstronger. Because of this weak outflow, low overnight temperatures\nwill continue to drop. This will bring low temperatures into the \n30s with the northern panhandle, becoming more likely to see lows \nin the mid to high 20s overnight. At the end of the weekend, a \nweak short wave will slightly increase precipitation chances over \nthe northern gulf coast. Any precipitation amounts will remain on \nthe lighter side with little to no forecasted accumulation \namounts.",
